    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1979, the Hivel Und Dahl Preservation Society preserves Old Zionsville’s early settlers, farming heritage, and town growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        19,
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/27051"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The society runs a research library open to the public, offering a wealth of historical documents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/27051"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its museum showcases artifacts, photographs, and documents that chronicle Old Zionsville’s regional history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/27051"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Old Zionsville sits along Pennsylvania State Routes 29 and 100, just 2.5 miles southeast of Macungie.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Zionsville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The village straddles the watershed divide between the Lehigh and Schuylkill Rivers, with northern areas draining to the Lehigh.",
